the-firm-as-one-program-15 : List Word
the-firm-as-one-program-15 = unlines (cons "- **P4** Existing languages and standards as data, with adequacy proofs (hyperactivity v31 §5, §8)." (cons "  A programming language is a record of syntax, judgments, configurations, steps and observations, and its meaning is one guarded unfolding. Fidelity to a published standard is an equivalence between the standard's derivations and the represented ones. C++ in full, with its distinctions between undefined, unspecified and implementation-defined behaviour, sits inside the host as data. Proofs attach to existing source as dependent pairs and erase back to the unchanged code (hyperactivity v31 §5, §8)." nil))
